Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.14.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.14.0 keeps the black-screen fix of 0.13.0 and removes the remaining one-frame flash on app switches. Archive 14 confirms the round-13 fix works: the user reports the floating window no longer goes black, and the log shows FBScene.foreground read back as 1 after setForeground:YES, so the app process is no longer suspended. Two residual causes of the flash remain in the log. First, deactivationReasons idles at 32 on this device while everything is healthy, so the preventive delta write reset it to 0 on every tick; each such write costs a full scene resubmission and buys nothing. Second, the user had turned on the escape hatch keepAlivePreventHard, which in 0.13.0 participated in the delta short-circuit, so the no-delta path never fired and updateSettingsWithBlock was called every single tick. 0.14.0 therefore does three things. First, the deactivationReasons write is verified by reading it back, and after keepAliveDeactFuse consecutive no-op writes (default 5) the tweak fuses that item off and never writes it again; setting the value to 0 disables the fuse for A/B work. Second, keepAlivePreventHard no longer counts as a delta: it only changes what a write contains, never whether one happens. Third, the black-screen recovery is now tiered: level 1 writes only the state items, level 2 adds the frame, level 3 adds displayConfiguration, escalating after three consecutive down ticks. Archive 14 shows real black episodes recovering in a single tick, so geometry rarely needs to be touched, and displayConfiguration is precisely the item that resets the frame to full screen and forces a second re-layout. New config keys: keepAliveDeactFuse = 5, keepAliveTieredRestore = true. For A/B work, keepAliveDeactFuse = 0 reproduces the 0.13.0 per-tick deact writes, and keepAliveTieredRestore = false restores the always-level-3 recovery of 0.13.0.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
